<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Parging in Calgary is the cement coat over the exposed foundation wall, the strip of concrete between the ground and the stucco or siding. Homeowners searching for parging Calgary usually mean one of three things: hairline cracks, a patch that has flaked off, or a coat that has gone hollow across a whole side after years of freeze-thaw. Sandstone Stucco Co is an advertising service that puts you in touch with independent Calgary stucco contractors, who quote and contract directly with you.</p><p>This page covers how parging fails, when a patch is enough and when a full-perimeter recoat is the more sensible scope, what a sound job involves, and the prices Calgary firms publish. It stops where the parging stops: cracks that run through the foundation, damp basements and structural movement belong to a different trade. To be introduced to a contractor for a no-obligation quote, call <strong>(403) 555-0148</strong>.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Patch or full recoat</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A defined chip or crack is a patch; a coat that is hollow or cracked along a whole wall is a recoat. The contractor who sees the wall decides the scope and should explain the choice.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Sound surface first</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Loose and hollow parging is taken back to solid concrete and the surface cleaned before anything new goes on. Ask how the contractor checks for hollow areas.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Bonding and mix named</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Ask which bonding agent or surface preparation, and which parging product and mix, the contractor will use. A named product has a manufacturer data sheet you can read.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Cure and weather</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Stucco base-coat manufacturers set minimum temperatures of 4°C to 5°C and a cure period. Ask how the contractor will handle a cold or wet week.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Colour and finish match</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Cement parging can be left as a plain grey coat or finished in acrylic. Matching a weathered wall is hard, and a contractor should say up front if a perfect match is not possible.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">A written scope</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Get the walls covered, product, finish, GST and payment terms in writing from more than one contractor, and you can compare quotes like for like.</p>
      </div>
</div>
